Linux OS
========

=> Linux is an open-source operating system ecosystem built around
the Linux kernel

=> Linux source code is available under open-source licensing

=> Linux servers are commonly administered using CLI

=> Linux supports multiple users and multiple processes

=> Linux provides strong security features such as

```
    User accounts
    Groups
    File permissions
    Ownership
    sudo
    Firewall
    SSH security
    Mandatory access control on supported distributions
```

=> Linux does not mean "antivirus is never required"

Note:
Security requirements depend on the environment, application,
threat model and company security policy.

=> Linux kernel was originally created by Linus Torvalds

=> Linux is widely used to manage servers

```
    Ex:
    Application Servers
    Database Servers
    Web Servers
    Docker
    Kubernetes
    Jenkins
    Nexus
    SonarQube
    Monitoring Servers
    Logging Servers
```

==============
Linux History
=============

-> Linus Torvalds started developing the Linux kernel in 1991

-> Linux was inspired by Unix-like operating systems and Minix

-> Linus Torvalds created the Linux kernel as a Unix-like operating
system kernel and released it under an open-source license

-> Linux later became the foundation for many operating systems
and distributions

Note:

The commonly taught explanation

```
    (Li)nus + Mi(nux) = Linux
```

is popular Linux history/lore, but Linux is more accurately understood
as the name of the kernel/project rather than simply a word combination.

=====================
Linux Distributions
===================

-> Linux is an open-source kernel

-> Different organizations and communities build complete operating
systems around the Linux kernel

-> These complete operating systems are called Linux Distributions

-> Different distributions provide their own:

```
    Package repositories
    Package management
    Default configurations
    Installer
    Security tools
    Support model
    Release lifecycle
```

-> We have many Linux distributions in the market

```
    Ex:
    Ubuntu
    Debian
    Red Hat Enterprise Linux
    Fedora
    SUSE
    Amazon Linux
    Kali Linux
    Rocky Linux
    AlmaLinux
```

