```

mkdir : Make directory

```
    mkdir velguru

    mkdir java python aws devops
```

rmdir : Remove empty directory

```
    rmdir devops
```

ls : List files/directories of present working directory

```
    ls -l
    Display detailed listing

    ls -lr
    Display detailed listing in reverse order

    ls -lt
    Display files based on modification time
    Latest files first

    ls -ltr
    Display files based on modification time
    Oldest files first

    ls -la
    Display hidden files also
```

cd : Change directory / navigation

```
    cd <dir-name>
    Go inside the directory

    cd ..
    Come out from current directory

    cd ~
    Go to current user's home directory
```

touch : To create empty files

```
    touch f1.txt

    touch f2.txt f3.txt f4.txt
```

cat : Create file with data + append data + print file data

```
    cat > f1.txt
    Create new file with data

    enter cntrl+d to save a

    cat >> f1.txt
    Append data to existing file

    cat f1.txt
    Print file data from top to bottom

    cat -n f1.txt
    Print file data along with line numbers
```

rm : Remove files/directories

```
    rm f1.txt
    Remove a file

    rm -r devops
    Remove a directory and its contents

    rm -rf devops
    Forcefully remove directory and its contents
```

Note:
Be very careful with `rm -rf`.

It can permanently delete data.

cp : Copy files/directories

```
    cp f1.txt f2.txt

    cp f1.txt devops/

    cp -r java devops/
```

Note:
To combine the contents of multiple files:

```
    cat f1.txt f2.txt > f3.txt
```

mv : Rename or move files/directories

```
    mv linux.txt linux-os.txt

    mv git.txt devops/

    mv java devops/
```

